# ============================================================
# CYBERDUDEBIVASH SENTINEL APEX — .assetsignore (Cloudflare Workers Static Assets)
# ============================================================
#
# Same purpose as .vercelignore, same gitignore-style syntax (Wrangler's
# own convention), different mechanism: this controls what gets uploaded
# to Cloudflare's static-asset layer when assets.directory points at the
# repo root. Wrangler will not upload anything matching a line here.
#
# The first block is copied verbatim from .vercelignore — same reasoning
# applies unchanged (see that file's header comment: CLAUDE.md and
# Sentinel-APEX/README.md were live and Google-indexed before that
# exclusion existed). Keep the two lists in sync if either changes.

CLAUDE.md
Sentinel-APEX/
eito/
platform/
prompts/
scripts/
docs/
marketing/
BUSINESS-TRANSFORMATION-ROADMAP-2026.md
AUDIT-REPORT-2026-05-28.md
OPERATIONS.md
RUNBOOKS.md
backups/

# --------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloudflare-specific additions below — not needed in .vercelignore
# because Vercel's build system already handles these automatically
# (its own api/** function-routing convention, and it never considers
# node_modules/.git part of the static bundle in the first place).
# Cloudflare's assets.directory has no equivalent auto-detection, so
# these need to be explicit or they would be served as literal static
# files.
# --------------------------------------------------------------

# Every api/**/*.js file is server-side handler/library source (dispatched
# by workers/entry.js via workers/lib/route-table.js), never a static
# asset. This deliberately does NOT exclude api/intel/**/*.json (static
# threat-intel data, meant to be publicly fetchable, exactly as it is on
# Vercel today) or non-.js data api/** may contain (e.g. bundled font
# assets api/og.js reads via the ASSETS binding instead of fs).
api/**/*.js

# Worker source itself — same category of internal implementation detail
# as scripts/ above, not meant to be publicly downloadable.
workers/

# Deploy tooling / VCS internals — never part of any site's content in any
# convention, regardless of what .vercelignore does or doesn't say.
node_modules/
.git/
.wrangler/
